GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\crimewidthkill\repair16_f2_20260926\f2_packet_codex_v2.md:700:**Grade: L2, the same as the DOG pair — not disclosed.** HARD_RESET is tested as a case (`if (idata & HARD_RESET)`), so it is in the CONTROL arm's generating set; the clear is that branch's repair; nulling a tested partition's repair is the canonical (d) mutant, and the round already graded the identical shape on DOG "L2, IN as the pair." Grading the twin lower would be the #499 two-of-a-two-by-two. Owed in-round, **test-first**: build D_noresetclear and show 218/218; add `ctlreset sw msg` / `ctlreset sd msg` (accepted `0x800` at +0x08 as the session's last access, count `CRIME_CONTROL: unimplemented` == 0, the halt `v1 == SENT` as the in-session liveness half so a dead channel cannot read 0 for free); show the pair reds the mutant, greens the fix, moves no other leg. Then close the class in the contract: each *tested* CONTROL bit carries a side-effect detector and a residue-print detector (DOG: ctldog + surv; HARD_RESET: rst + ctlreset).
