GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbdrainwire_20260924\fable5_final.md:5:**No verdict-level ruling changes: P_win stays clause (e), deepseek stays overruled, the chain closes on the closing pass.** What changes is records: **4 of 15 closing-pass dispositions are wrong**, all four in the drafts or the contract text, none needing code or a re-table. The ledger script **crashes** (measured), two CHANGELOG sentences are false, one measured escape is missing from the gate block's contract, and #442's own CHANGELOG block still carries no late-finding line.
GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbdrainwire_20260924\fable5_final.md:9:**1. P_win: clause (e), FILE — upheld, but the round's stated reason is the wrong one.** Both `==` and `count >= bound && count <= bound + W` are clause-(d)-shaped ("a condition qualified"); what decides L2 versus (e) is whether the exempted region is a floor cell. The floor on the count axis is the body's own test, one relational operator, and the generating set of a relational operator is the three regions its neighbours differ on: below, at, past. `==` (an operator substitution) exempts the *past* region — a generating-set cell, unrowed at #442 — so L2. P_win adds a **second boundary at a constant the body never tests**; that is the `&& idata != k` shape the carrier already grades clause (e) (pcc2 pass 11: "a value the body never tests as a case"). The consequence argument must be rejected, and not only for the #392 reason: a consequence-keyed floor makes M_zge, M_neqB and M_upskip L2 too (each returns the same debt through a re-arm), i.e. rulings 1 and 2 stand or fall together, and deepseek would be right. Write the generating-set reason into the CHANGELOG's dissent line; "escaped a cell that was NOT rowed / splits a cell that is" is true but not derivable by reading. Two corrections to the filing: the closure must owe the **ceiling, 68,157,440** — a 50 MHz pre-charge caps at 50,000,000 (`c_harness.txt` R5 case) and leaves every W in [50e6−762, ceiling) alive and non-equivalent — so R6's pre-charge arm needs a high-hz case like R1's; and P_win's consequence is the #442 dead clock itself (accrue near the ceiling at 31.5 s, re-arm to 50 MHz, overflow ~42 s later), so keep it MED and first in `fbbounddebt`. Cost of the constant is comparable to R1's existing 28 ceiling-length drives; taking it now would be a fifth revision owing its own pass, which is exactly why (e) files at closure.
GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbdrainwire_20260924\fable5_final.md:13:**3. Wrong dispositions, 4 of 15.** The contract texts are true sentence by sentence: R6's comment (8192 past every new bound; `==` agrees below and at; the 4529 figures match `opus5_p1b`/`opus5_f2`; end counts ((8192−1) mod B)+1 = 572/567/2090/2089 recomputed; the unconditioned store; the P_win paragraph matches `c_rung3_pwin.txt` 49603 and `c_blocks.txt` 41/41), the R5 comment (50,000,000 = 0x2FAF080 has bit 17 set and bit 16 clear, so the mask lowers timers 2–3 only, and 63,750,000 = 0x3CCBF70 and the ceiling have both clear — one red case, matching M_mask16 R5=1), and the gate block (3051 on all four in `c_blocks.txt`; M_x8 3051 and M_f16 3/3 on all four in `p2/table2_part2_blocks.txt`; 1183/385 in `results_table.txt`; `>`, reset-to-0 and reset-to-2 arithmetic checks; `_opt()`). The four wrong:
GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbdrainwire_20260924\fable5_final.md:14:- **(a)** CHANGELOG and this brief: "the Opus seat: 18 new mutants …, all red" — `c_harness.txt` lists 18 P_/R_/S_ mutants: 16 red, R_bnd red only through gate 2's R6 pin, **P_win green everywhere**. The mutant this brief asks me to rule on is recorded as killed.
GXEMUL-SEC\regress\artifacts\fbdrainwire_20260924\fable5_final.md:15:- **(b)** CHANGELOG: "26 mutants … every mutant red except the three store guards and the window mutant" — seven of the 26 pass gate 2's harness: also M_en, M_en0 (caught by gate 14's arm X), M_nper, M_f16 (caught by nothing, filed). P_win is not among the 26.
